        "original_id": "feb5957b-8e22-56ad-9f2a-2c269202c056",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Adelaide Laetitia \"Addie\" Miethke\n- Organizations: School of the Air, Royal Flying Doctor Service\n- Places: South Australia, Australia\n- Topics: remote education, correspondence schooling, radio-based instruction, internet-based instruction\n\nFacts:\n- Adelaide Laetitia \"Addie\" Miethke was born on 8 June 1881.\n- Adelaide Laetitia \"Addie\" Miethke was a South Australian educator and teacher.\n- Adelaide Laetitia \"Addie\" Miethke was pivotal in the formation of the School of the Air.\n- The School of the Air was formed using the existing Royal Flying Doctor Service radio network.\n- School of the Air is a generic term for correspondence schools serving primary and early secondary children in remote and outback Australia.\n- School of the Air traditionally conducted some or all classes by radio.\n- School of the Air has increasingly replaced radio-based instruction with internet technology.\n- Adelaide Laetitia \"Addie\" Miethke died on 4 February 1962.",
